<LegalPage
  appName="Appelou"
  docTitle="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Appelou handles your data: what the app collects, why, who processes it, and your rights under the LGPD and GDPR."
  canonicalUrl="https://rubenspessoa.dev/appelou/privacy/"
  effectiveDate="July 22, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what data the Appelou app for iPhone collects, why, who processes it, and
    the rights you have. Appelou compares real-time retail prices for shoppers in Alagoas, Brazil.
    The app works without an account and we do not sell your personal data. Because Appelou is
    distributed in Brazil, this policy is written to satisfy both the Brazilian LGPD and the
    European GDPR.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    Rubens Pessoa de Barros Filho
    <br />
    UNESCO-Esplanade 8/55, 8020 Graz, Austria
    <br />
    Email: <a href="mailto:contact@rubenspessoa.dev">contact@rubenspessoa.dev</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    See the <a href="/imprint/">imprint</a> for full legal details.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect and why</h2>

  <h3>Searches</h3>
  <p>
    When you search for a product, your search query is sent to our servers to return matching
    offers. Search is powered by Algolia (USA). Queries are not tied to your name or identity.
  </p>

  <h3>Location</h3>
  <p>
    With your permission, the app uses your device location to show offers from stores near you.
    Location is used while you use the app to run nearby searches; it is not used to build a
    movement profile. You can revoke this permission at any time in iOS Settings, and the app
    keeps working with a manually chosen region.
  </p>

  <h3>Advertising</h3>
  <p>
    The free tier shows ads served by Google AdMob (USA). If you allow tracking in the iOS
    App Tracking Transparency prompt (and, where required, consent through the Google consent
    dialog), Google may use identifiers such as the advertising ID to personalize ads; if you
    decline, ads are non-personalized. Google acts as an independent controller for ad serving;
    see
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google&rsquo;s advertising policy</a>
    for details. Subscribing removes ads.
  </p>

  <h3>Install attribution</h3>
  <p>
    We use AppsFlyer (with servers in the USA/EU) to understand which marketing campaigns lead to
    app installs and subscriptions. AppsFlyer processes device identifiers and technical signals
    for this, subject to your App Tracking Transparency choice.
  </p>

  <h3>Purchases</h3>
  <p>
    Subscriptions are sold and billed by Apple through the App Store. We never see your payment
    details. RevenueCat (USA) processes your App Store transaction status together with an
    anonymous identifier so the app knows whether your subscription is active.
  </p>

  <h3>Usage analytics and crash reports</h3>
  <p>
    We use Google Firebase Analytics and Firebase services (USA) to understand how the app is used
    (screens viewed, features used) and to collect crash and error reports (device model, OS
    version, stack traces). Analytics are keyed to an anonymous identifier; we cannot identify you
    personally from it.
  </p>

  <h2>Legal bases</h2>
  <p>
    Under the GDPR and LGPD we process data based on: <strong>performance of a contract</strong>
    (running your searches and providing your subscription), <strong>legitimate interest</strong>
    (product analytics, crash reporting, non-personalized ads, fraud prevention), and
    <strong>consent</strong> (location access, personalized advertising, and tracking-based
    attribution).
  </p>

  <h2>Who processes data for us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Apple (USA): App Store distribution, payments, device services</li>
    <li>Google Firebase (USA): server infrastructure, analytics, crash reporting</li>
    <li>Google AdMob (USA): advertising</li>
    <li>Algolia (USA): product search</li>
    <li>AppsFlyer (USA/EU): install attribution</li>
    <li>RevenueCat (USA): subscription status</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Where providers are located outside Brazil or the EU, transfers rely on the EU-US Data Privacy
    Framework, Standard Contractual Clauses, or equivalent safeguards under the LGPD.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Search queries: kept in short-lived technical logs, not tied to your identity</li>
    <li>Location: used at query time; not stored as a location history on our servers</li>
    <li>
      Analytics, attribution, and crash data: per the retention settings of the respective tool,
      kept only as long as needed for the purposes above
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under the LGPD and GDPR you have the right to access, rectify, delete, restrict, or receive a
    copy of your data, to object to processing based on legitimate interest, and to withdraw
    consent at any time (for tracking and location, directly in iOS Settings). Because we hold no
    account for you, exercising these rights works by email: write to
    <a href="mailto:contact@rubenspessoa.dev">contact@rubenspessoa.dev</a>. You may also complain
    to the Brazilian data protection authority (ANPD), the Austrian Data Protection Authority (
    <a href="https://www.dsb.gv.at" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">dsb.gv.at</a>), or
    your local supervisory authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Appelou is not directed at children under 14, and we do not knowingly collect data from them.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy, we will update it here with a new effective date. Material changes
    will be highlighted in the app.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
